content.text:
Use the `@variant` directive in your CSS with the breakpoint name (`src/docs/functions-and-directives.mdx`, "@variant"). The docs only show it with `dark`, but breakpoints are variants too, so this should work:

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;
  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

Alternatively, write a plain media query. Each breakpoint maps to `@media (width >= 48rem)` for `md`, for example (`src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, breakpoint table). Custom breakpoints defined with `--breakpoint-*` in `@theme` get their own variants (`responsive-design.mdx`, "Using custom breakpoints").

I didn't find an example of `@variant` with a breakpoint, or of `theme(--breakpoint-md)` inside a media query.

